      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C08"],
      "claim": "Compound 3l, a related heteroaryl system with fluorophenyl and heterocyclic substituents, showed an estimated steady-state brain/plasma ratio of 37 in rats, indicating excellent brain penetration for this structural class.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "A PET study in cynomolgus monkeys showed poor total brain uptake (0.8% ID) for a related indole/triazole radioligand; this contradictory observation is species- and radiotracer-specific and is outweighed by multiple direct supportive BBB-permeation records.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted pass: multiple direct BBB-permeation records in rats, mice, and humans for structurally related lipophilic halogenated fused heteroaromatics outweigh the few contradictory polar/radioligand-specific poor-uptake observations; the query's neutral, lipophilic thioether/dichlorophenyl profile is consistent with meaningful CNS access.",
